    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n36757" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pneumătĭcus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πνευματικός</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to air</i> or
				<i>to wind</i>, <i>air-</i>, <i>wind-</i>, <i>pneumatic;</i> of
			machines that are driven by the force of air: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ctesibius, qui pneumaticas res invenit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vitr. 9,
					9</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">organa,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					19, 4, 20, § 60</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ratio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 7,
					37, 38, § 125</span></i>
			.</div>
